	(text "The simple solution is to put the LED resistor, the LED and the button in a row, and connect the I/O between LED and button.\n\nThe I/O is set to open drain output, meaning only the pull transistor is ever activated. Now you can read the pin to sample the button while the output circuit is floating, and turn on the LED on by putting the output circuit to low."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 143.51 154.432 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "a9f8bc25-7139-4ec9-85ac-41234bb7514f")
	)
